module

public import Feec.Ch4.BoxRestrict
public import Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvageMax

/-!
# Prop 4.17 on a box with the thesis' boundary conditions: only static data propagate

Thesis Prop 4.17 ([QuennevilleBelair2015, §4.10]) is stated on a bounded domain `Ω ⊂ ℝ³` for the
complex `H̊¹(V) → H̊(curl; M) → L²(M)`, i.e. with the boundary conditions `σ = 0`,
`E_a × n = 0` (row-wise) and no condition on `B`. `Feec.Ch4.BoundedDomain` and
`Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvage` show that TSD propagation fails there, and
`Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvageMax` replaces `K = {0} × L²(TSD) × L²(TSD)` by its largest invariant
subspace `K*`, leaving open whether `K*` contains any non-stationary datum. This file settles that
question on the box `Q = (0, ½)³`, in the parity model described below: **`K*` consists exactly
of the stationary data in `K`**, namely `(0, 0, B₀)` with `B₀ ∈ L²(TSD)` curl-free (for instance
the constant `diag(1, -1, 0)`, `Feec.Box.staticB_mem_Kmax`, and the linearly independent
`e₀e₁ᵀ + e₁e₀ᵀ`, `Feec.Box.offB_mem_Kmax`; non-constant Hessians of harmonic functions are
further examples, not formalized here). So no non-stationary datum has its whole orbit
(`t ∈ ℝ`, as in the definition of `K*`) in `K`. The forward-only version (`t ≥ 0`), which is
weaker in general (see the correction in `Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvageMax`), also holds on the box:
`Feec.Box.forward_boxTSD_iff` (in `Feec.Ch4.BoxIdent`), a consequence of the pure point spectrum
of the torus wave group and the mean ergodic theorem (`Feec.Models.Cube.Parity.forward_tsd_iff`).

## The box model (method of images)

`Q` is a fundamental domain of the group generated by the reflections `x_i ↦ -x_i` of
`𝕋³ = ℝ³/ℤ³`. Each component of a field on `Q` extends to `𝕋³` with a prescribed parity in
each variable, and the boundary conditions of the thesis' complex are encoded by these parities
(odd in `x_i` = Dirichlet on the faces `x_i ∈ {0, ½}`, even = no condition for the derivatives
involved):
* `σ_a` odd in every variable (`σ ∈ H̊¹`): `ParV`;
* `E_{ab}` even in `x_b`, odd in the other variables (`E_a × n = 0`, `E ∈ H̊(curl)` row-wise):
  `ParRow 1`;
* `B_{ab}` odd in `x_b`, even in the other variables (`B ∈ H(curl)`, no condition): `ParRow (-1)`.
On Fourier coefficients the parity of `f` in `x_i` is `f̂(R_i k) = ± f̂(k)`, `R_i` the reflection
of the `i`-th index (`refl`). The periodic operators `grad`, `curl`, `div` of `Feec.Ch4.Torus` map
these parity classes into each other exactly as the box complex requires, and the periodic group
`Feec.Torus.periodicGroup` preserves the parity space (`periodicGroup_mem_Par`), so the box
dynamics is the periodic dynamics restricted to `Par`.

The constraints are imposed **on the box**, not on `𝕋³`: entries of different parities
are compared through their restrictions to `Q` (`Feec.Box.ZeroOnBox`), since the extensions of
`E_{ab}` and `E_{ba}` have different parities. `boxSym`, `boxTr`, `boxDiv`: symmetric, trace-free,
divergence-free on `Q` (the divergence weakly, against smooth test functions with support in
`Q`); `boxTSD τ = ParRow τ ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr ⊓ boxDiv`.

Normalization: `𝕋³` has volume `1` and `Q` volume `1/8`, so on each parity class the `L²(𝕋³)`
inner product is `8` times the `L²(Q)` inner product of the restrictions; the factor is the same
in every slot and does not affect adjoints, the Hodge wave operator or invariant subspaces.

Identification: `Feec.Ch4.BoxIdent` proves that, for real fields, restriction to `Q` is a
bijection (norms scaled by `8^{-1/2}`, operators intertwined) from these parity spaces onto the
bounded-domain spaces of `Feec.Ch4.BoundedDomain` for `Ω = Q`: `ParV ∩ H¹` onto `H̊¹(Q)`,
`ParRow 1 ∩ H(curl)` onto `H̊(curl, Q)`, `ParRow (-1) ∩ H(curl)` onto `H(curl, Q)`,
`ParRow 1 ∩ H(div)` onto `H(div, Q)` and `boxTSD (±1)` onto `L²(TSD)(Q)`
(`Feec.BoxIdent.bijOn_resB_HcurlZero`, `Feec.BoxIdent.bijOn_resBV_H1Zero`, ...), and transfers the
results below to `Feec.BoundedDomain.thesisComplex` on `Q` and on every open cube
(`Feec.BoxIdent.openCube_mem_Kmax_iff'`). That file does not identify the even (Neumann) or
mirror parity classes.

## Main results

* Fibre algebra of the symbol `W_ξ` of `-L`: `tot_waveSym_sq`
  (`W_ξ² = -|ξ|² + (0, 0, (ρξ)ξᵀ)`), `waveSym_four` (`W_ξ⁴ = -|ξ|² W_ξ²`),
  `eq_zero_of_waveSym_sq` (the only eigenvalue of `-W_ξ²` besides `0` is `|ξ|²`).
* `eq_zero_of_parRow_of_finite`: a trigonometric polynomial matrix field in `ParRow τ` that is
  symmetric and trace-free on `Q` vanishes. (The extensions of `E_{ab}` and `E_{ba}` have
  different parities, and so do those of the diagonal entries; on trigonometric polynomials
  equality on `Q` propagates to `𝕋³` by analyticity, `eq_zero_of_zeroOnBox_of_finite`.)
* Spectral splitting of `K*` without spectral theory: `K*` is reducing for the group, so its
  projection commutes with `L` (`Feec.Constraints.reducing_of_invariant`) and preserves each
  eigenspace `N_ω = ker(L² + ω²)` (`starProjection_mem_N`), so the `N_ω`-component of a datum in
  `K*` is again in `K*` (`starProjection_N_mem`). For `ω > 0` that component is a trigonometric
  polynomial in `K`, hence `0` (`eq_zero_of_mem_Kmax_N`); so every `x ∈ K*` is killed by every
  symbol, `W_k x̂(k) = 0` (`waveSym_eq_zero_of_mem_Kmax`).
* **`mem_Kmax_iff`**: for any closed `S1 ≤ ParRow 1 ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr`,
  `S2 ≤ ParRow (-1) ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr`, `x ∈ K*` iff `x ∈ K` and `x` is stationary
  (`S t x = x` for all `t`).
* **`mem_Kmax_boxTSD_iff`** (the thesis' `K`): `x ∈ K*` iff `x = (0, 0, B₀)` with
  `B₀ ∈ boxTSD (-1)` and `curl B₀ = 0`. In particular `S1* = 0`.

Related files: `Feec.Ch4.BoxThesis` builds the box complex as a Hilbert complex in its own right
(`Feec.Box.thesisBoxComplex`) and proves the same characterization of `K*` for every orthogonal
group generated by its Hodge wave operator (`Feec.Box.thesisBox_mem_Kmax_iff`);
`Feec.Ch4.BoxStatic` shows `K* ≠ 0` (it contains `(0, 0, diag(1, -1, 0))`,
`Feec.Box.staticB_mem_Kmax`); `Feec.Ch4.BoxMirror` shows that with tensorial mirror boundary
conditions Props 4.17 and 4.19 hold on the box.

Correction (to the research notes in `Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvageMax`): the expected answer
"`S1* = 0`, `S2* = L²(TSD) ∩ ker curl`" is confirmed on the box. The proof does not need the
spectral theorem for the bounded-domain Maxwell operator: the eigenvector expansion is explicit on
the Fourier side, and the comparison of sine and cosine profiles is the analytic continuation of
trigonometric polynomials from `Q` to `𝕋³`. Divergence-freeness is not used: symmetry and
trace-freeness on `Q` already force every non-stationary mode to vanish.

## References

* [QuennevilleBelair2015], §4.10 (Prop 4.17, (4.14)), §3.4 (Lemma 3.5)
* [AFW2010] (Hilbert complexes)
* [Pazy1983], §1.10 (unitary groups, reducing subspaces)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace InnerProductSpace ENNReal
open MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology LinearPMap NormedSpace

namespace Feec.Box

open Feec.Torus Feec.TorusWeak Feec.Constraints HilbertComplex2

attribute [local instance] Feec.Torus.instMeasureSpaceUnitAddCircle_feec

/-! ## Fibre algebra of the wave symbol -/

section Fibre

/-- `div_ξ (c ξᵀ) = |ξ|² c`. -/
theorem divR_outer (ξ : Freq) (c : Vec3) : divR ξ (outer c ξ) = (‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • c := by
  ext a
  simp only [divR_apply, outer, mat_apply, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, norm_sq_freq,
    Fin.sum_univ_three]
  push_cast; ring

/-- **The square of the wave symbol**: `W_ξ²(σ, u, ρ) = (-|ξ|² σ, -|ξ|² u, -|ξ|² ρ + (ρξ)ξᵀ)`
(`div grad = -|ξ|²`, `grad div - curl curl = -|ξ|²` on matrices, and `curl curl ρ = |ξ|² ρ -
(ρξ)ξᵀ` on the last slot, where the complex stops). -/
theorem tot_waveSym_sq (ξ : Freq) (x : Fib) :
    tot _ _ _ (waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ x)) =
      (-(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • (tot _ _ _ x).1, -(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • (tot _ _ _ x).2.1,
        -(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • (tot _ _ _ x).2.2 + outer (divR ξ (tot _ _ _ x).2.2) ξ) := by
  rw [tot_waveSym, tot_waveSym]
  obtain ⟨σ, u, ρ⟩ := tot _ _ _ x
  simp only
  rw [norm_sq_freq]
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_)
  · ext a
    simp only [PiLp.neg_apply, PiLp.sub_apply, divSym_apply, gradSym_apply, curlSym_apply,
      jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, Fin.sum_univ_three]
    fin_cases a <;> simp <;> ring_nf <;> simp [Complex.I_sq] <;> ring
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩
    simp only [PiLp.neg_apply, PiLp.sub_apply, divSym_apply, gradSym_apply, curlSym_apply,
      jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, Fin.sum_univ_three,
      _root_.map_neg]
    fin_cases b <;> simp <;> ring_nf <;> simp [Complex.I_sq] <;> ring
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩
    simp only [PiLp.neg_apply, PiLp.sub_apply, PiLp.add_apply, gradSym_apply, curlSym_apply,
      jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, Fin.sum_univ_three,
      _root_.map_neg, _root_.map_sub, outer, mat_apply, divR_apply]
    fin_cases b <;> simp <;> ring_nf <;> simp [Complex.I_sq] <;> ring

/-- `W_ξ⁴ = -|ξ|² W_ξ²`: the range of `W_ξ` is the `|ξ|²`-eigenspace of `-W_ξ²`. -/
theorem waveSym_four (ξ : Freq) (x : Fib) :
    waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ x))) =
      -(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ x) := by
  apply (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective
  rw [tot_waveSym_sq, LinearEquiv.map_smul, tot_waveSym_sq]
  obtain ⟨σ, u, ρ⟩ := tot _ _ _ x
  simp only [_root_.map_add, _root_.map_smul, divR_outer, Prod.smul_mk]
  refine Prod.ext rfl (Prod.ext rfl ?_)
  simp only
  have : -(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • divR ξ ρ + (‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • divR ξ ρ = 0 := by
    rw [neg_smul, neg_add_cancel]
  rw [this]
  have h0 : outer 0 ξ = 0 := by ext ⟨a, b⟩; simp [outer]
  rw [h0, add_zero, smul_add]

/-- **Eigenvalues of `-W_ξ²`**: if `W_ξ² v = -ω² v` with `ω > 0`, then `v = 0` unless
`|ξ| = ω`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_waveSym_sq {ξ : Freq} {ω : ℝ} (hω : 0 < ω) (hne : ‖ξ‖ ≠ ω) {v : Fib}
    (h : waveSym ξ (waveSym ξ v) = -(ω ^ 2) • v) : v = 0 := by
  have h2 : ‖ξ‖ ^ 2 ≠ ω ^ 2 := fun e =>
    hne ((sq_eq_sq₀ (norm_nonneg _) hω.le).1 e)
  have hc : (ω ^ 2 - ‖ξ‖ ^ 2) ≠ 0 := sub_ne_zero.2 (Ne.symm h2)
  have ht := congrArg (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3) h
  rw [tot_waveSym_sq, LinearEquiv.map_smul] at ht
  rcases hx : tot _ _ _ v with ⟨σ, u, ρ⟩
  rw [hx] at ht
  simp only [Prod.smul_mk, Prod.mk.injEq] at ht
  obtain ⟨e1, e2, e3⟩ := ht
  have key : ∀ {E : Type} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E] (w : E),
      -(‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • w = -(ω ^ 2) • w → w = 0 := by
    intro E _ _ w e
    rw [neg_smul, neg_smul, neg_inj] at e
    have : (ω ^ 2 - ‖ξ‖ ^ 2) • w = 0 := by rw [sub_smul, e, sub_self]
    exact (smul_eq_zero.1 this).resolve_left hc
  have hd : divR ξ ρ = 0 := by
    have e4 := congrArg (divR ξ) e3
    rw [_root_.map_add, _root_.map_smul, _root_.map_smul, divR_outer, neg_smul, neg_add_cancel,
      eq_comm,
      neg_smul, neg_eq_zero] at e4
    exact (smul_eq_zero.1 e4).resolve_left (pow_ne_zero 2 hω.ne')
  have h0 : outer 0 ξ = 0 := by ext ⟨a, b⟩; simp [outer]
  rw [hd, h0, add_zero] at e3
  apply (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective
  rw [hx, key σ e1, key u e2, key ρ e3, _root_.map_zero]
  rfl

/-- At `ξ = 0` the wave symbol vanishes. -/
theorem waveSym_zero (x : Fib) : waveSym 0 x = 0 := by
  apply (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective
  rw [tot_waveSym, _root_.map_zero]
  obtain ⟨σ, u, ρ⟩ := tot _ _ _ x
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_)
  · ext a; simp [divSym_apply]
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩; fin_cases b <;> simp [gradSym_apply, curlSym_apply, jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross]
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩; fin_cases b <;> simp [curlSym_apply, jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross]

end Fibre

/-! ## Parities and the box conditions -/

section Parity

/-- The reflection `R_i` of the `i`-th frequency index (the Fourier side of `x_i ↦ -x_i`). -/
def refl (i : Fin 3) (k : Z3) : Z3 := Function.update k i (-(k i))

/-- `R_i` is an involution. -/
@[simp] theorem refl_refl (i : Fin 3) (k : Z3) : refl i (refl i k) = k := by
  ext j
  by_cases h : j = i
  · subst h; simp [refl]
  · simp [refl, Function.update_of_ne h]

/-- `R_i 0 = 0`. -/
@[simp] theorem refl_zero (i : Fin 3) : refl i 0 = 0 := by
  ext j; by_cases h : j = i
  · subst h; simp [refl]
  · simp [refl, Function.update_of_ne h]

/-- `colSign i b = 1` if `b = i`, `-1` otherwise: the parity in `x_i` of the column-`b` entries of
an electric field (`E_{ab}` is even in `x_b` and odd in the other variables). -/
def colSign (i b : Fin 3) : ℂ := if i = b then 1 else -1

/-- **Row-wise parity classes** `ParRow τ`: `A_{ab}` has parity `τ · colSign i b` in `x_i`, i.e.
`Â(R_i k)_{ab} = τ colSign i b Â(k)_{ab}`. `ParRow 1` encodes the row-wise electric condition
(`E_a × n = 0` on `∂Q`, `E ∈ H̊(curl)`), `ParRow (-1)` the magnetic slot (`B ∈ H(curl)`, no
condition). -/
def ParRow (τ : ℂ) : Submodule ℝ L2M where
  carrier := {A | ∀ i k a b, A (refl i k) (a, b) = τ * colSign i b * A k (a, b)}
  zero_mem' := by intro i k a b; simp
  add_mem' := by
    intro A B hA hB i k a b
    simp only [lp.coeFn_add, Pi.add_apply, PiLp.add_apply, hA i k a b, hB i k a b]
    ring
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r A hA i k a b
    simp only [lp.coeFn_smul, Pi.smul_apply, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, hA i k a b]
    ring

/-- Membership in `ParRow τ`. -/
theorem mem_ParRow {τ : ℂ} {A : L2M} :
    A ∈ ParRow τ ↔ ∀ i k a b, A (refl i k) (a, b) = τ * colSign i b * A k (a, b) := Iff.rfl

/-- The Dirichlet parity class of vector fields (`σ ∈ H̊¹`): every component odd in every
variable. -/
def ParV : Submodule ℝ L2V where
  carrier := {σ | ∀ i k a, σ (refl i k) a = -σ k a}
  zero_mem' := by intro i k a; simp
  add_mem' := by
    intro σ ρ hσ hρ i k a
    simp only [lp.coeFn_add, Pi.add_apply, PiLp.add_apply, hσ i k a, hρ i k a]
    ring
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r σ hσ i k a
    simp only [lp.coeFn_smul, Pi.smul_apply, PiLp.smul_apply, Complex.real_smul, hσ i k a]
    ring

/-- Evaluation of a matrix-field coefficient is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_coef (k : Z3) (p : Fin 3 × Fin 3) : Continuous fun A : L2M => A k p :=
  (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℂ) p).continuous.comp
    (lp.evalCLM ℝ (fun _ : Z3 => Mat3) 2 k).continuous

/-- Evaluation of a vector-field coefficient is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_coefV (k : Z3) (a : Fin 3) : Continuous fun σ : L2V => σ k a :=
  (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℂ) a).continuous.comp
    (lp.evalCLM ℝ (fun _ : Z3 => Vec3) 2 k).continuous

/-- The parity classes are closed. -/
theorem isClosed_ParRow (τ : ℂ) : IsClosed (ParRow τ : Set L2M) := by
  have e : (ParRow τ : Set L2M) = ⋂ i, ⋂ k, ⋂ a, ⋂ b,
      {A : L2M | A (refl i k) (a, b) = τ * colSign i b * A k (a, b)} := by
    ext A; simp [mem_ParRow]
  rw [e]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun i => isClosed_iInter fun k => isClosed_iInter fun a =>
    isClosed_iInter fun b => isClosed_eq (continuous_coef _ _)
      (continuous_const.mul (continuous_coef _ _))

/-- The Dirichlet parity class is closed. -/
theorem isClosed_ParV : IsClosed (ParV : Set L2V) := by
  have e : (ParV : Set L2V) = ⋂ i, ⋂ k, ⋂ a, {σ : L2V | σ (refl i k) a = -σ k a} := by
    ext σ; simp [ParV]
  rw [e]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun i => isClosed_iInter fun k => isClosed_iInter fun a =>
    isClosed_eq (continuous_coefV _ _) (continuous_coefV _ _).neg

/-- Evaluation of an `ℓ²` sum. -/
theorem lp_sum_apply {ι α : Type*} {F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F]
    (s : Finset α) (g : α → L2 ι F) (k : ι) :
    (∑ a ∈ s, g a : L2 ι F) k = ∑ a ∈ s, g a k := by
  change lp.evalCLM ℝ (fun _ : ι => F) 2 k (∑ a ∈ s, g a) =
    ∑ a ∈ s, lp.evalCLM ℝ (fun _ : ι => F) 2 k (g a)
  exact _root_.map_sum _ _ _

/-- The entry `A_p` of a matrix field, as a scalar coefficient sequence. -/
def entry (p : Fin 3 × Fin 3) : L2M →L[ℝ] L2 Z3 ℂ :=
  ((PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : Fin 3 × Fin 3 => L2 Z3 ℂ) p).comp
    (swapL2 (ι := Z3) (P := Fin 3 × Fin 3)).symm.toContinuousLinearEquiv.toContinuousLinearMap
    ).restrictScalars ℝ

/-- Coefficients of `entry p A`. -/
@[simp] theorem entry_apply (p : Fin 3 × Fin 3) (A : L2M) (k : Z3) : entry p A k = A k p := rfl

/-- **Symmetric on the box**: `A_{ab} = A_{ba}` a.e. on `Q`. -/
def boxSym : Submodule ℝ L2M :=
  ⨅ a : Fin 3, ⨅ b : Fin 3, (boxZero.restrictScalars ℝ).comap
    (entry (a, b) - entry (b, a) : L2M →L[ℝ] L2 Z3 ℂ).toLinearMap

/-- **Trace-free on the box**: `Σ_a A_{aa} = 0` a.e. on `Q`. -/
def boxTr : Submodule ℝ L2M :=
  (boxZero.restrictScalars ℝ).comap (∑ a : Fin 3, entry (a, a) : L2M →L[ℝ] L2 Z3 ℂ).toLinearMap

theorem mem_boxSym {A : L2M} : A ∈ boxSym ↔ ∀ a b, ZeroOnBox (entry (a, b) A - entry (b, a) A) := by
  simp only [boxSym, Submodule.mem_iInf, Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem,
    mem_boxZero, ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe, _root_.sub_apply]

theorem mem_boxTr {A : L2M} : A ∈ boxTr ↔ ZeroOnBox (∑ a : Fin 3, entry (a, a) A) := by
  simp only [boxTr, Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, mem_boxZero,
    ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe, FunLike.coe_sum, Finset.sum_apply]

theorem isClosed_boxSym : IsClosed (boxSym : Set L2M) := by
  rw [boxSym, Submodule.coe_iInf]
  refine isClosed_iInter fun a => ?_
  rw [Submodule.coe_iInf]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun b => isClosed_boxZero.preimage (entry (a, b) - entry (b, a)).continuous

theorem isClosed_boxTr : IsClosed (boxTr : Set L2M) :=
  isClosed_boxZero.preimage (∑ a : Fin 3, entry (a, a)).continuous

/-- `∫ f ψ = ⟪ψ̄, f⟫` for continuous `ψ`: the bilinear pairing is continuous in `f`. -/
theorem integral_mul_eq_inner (f : L2T) {ψ : T3 → ℂ} (hψ : Continuous ψ) :
    ∫ x, (f : T3 → ℂ) x * ψ x =
      ⟪toL2 (Complex.continuous_conj.comp hψ), f⟫_ℂ := by
  rw [MeasureTheory.L2.inner_def]
  refine integral_congr_ae ?_
  refine (toL2_ae_eq (Complex.continuous_conj.comp hψ)).mono fun x hx => ?_
  dsimp only
  rw [RCLike.inner_apply, hx]
  simp

/-- Smooth test functions supported in the box: `C_c^∞(Q)`. -/
def BoxTest : Type := {φ : T3 → ℂ // IsSmooth φ ∧ tsupport φ ⊆ boxSet}

/-- The weak divergence pairing of row `a` against a test function:
`A ↦ Σ_b ∫ A_{ab} ∂_b φ`. -/
def divPair (a : Fin 3) (φ : BoxTest) : L2M →L[ℝ] ℂ :=
  ∑ b : Fin 3, ((innerSL ℂ (toL2 (Complex.continuous_conj.comp
    (continuous_partialT φ.2.1.contDiff_one b)))).restrictScalars ℝ).comp
    (((UnitAddTorus.mFourierBasis (d := Fin 3)).repr.symm.toContinuousLinearEquiv
      |>.toContinuousLinearMap.restrictScalars ℝ).comp (entry (a, b)))

/-- `divPair` is the weak divergence pairing. -/
theorem divPair_apply (a : Fin 3) (φ : BoxTest) (A : L2M) :
    divPair a φ A = ∑ b : Fin 3, ∫ x, (ofCoeff (entry (a, b) A) : T3 → ℂ) x * partialT b φ.1 x := by
  simp only [divPair, FunLike.coe_sum, Finset.sum_apply]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun b _ => ?_
  rw [integral_mul_eq_inner _ (continuous_partialT φ.2.1.contDiff_one b)]
  rfl

/-- **Divergence-free on the box** (row-wise, weakly): `Σ_b ∫_Q A_{ab} ∂_b φ = 0` for every
smooth `φ` with compact support in `Q`. -/
def boxDiv : Submodule ℝ L2M :=
  ⨅ a : Fin 3, ⨅ φ : BoxTest, LinearMap.ker (divPair a φ : L2M →ₗ[ℝ] ℂ)

theorem mem_boxDiv {A : L2M} : A ∈ boxDiv ↔ ∀ a (φ : T3 → ℂ), IsSmooth φ → tsupport φ ⊆ boxSet →
    ∑ b : Fin 3, ∫ x, (ofCoeff (entry (a, b) A) : T3 → ℂ) x * partialT b φ x = 0 := by
  simp only [boxDiv, Submodule.mem_iInf, LinearMap.mem_ker]
  constructor
  · intro h a φ h1 h2
    rw [← divPair_apply a ⟨φ, h1, h2⟩]; exact h a ⟨φ, h1, h2⟩
  · intro h a φ
    change divPair a φ A = 0
    rw [divPair_apply]; exact h a φ.1 φ.2.1 φ.2.2

theorem isClosed_boxDiv : IsClosed (boxDiv : Set L2M) := by
  rw [boxDiv, Submodule.coe_iInf]
  refine isClosed_iInter fun a => ?_
  rw [Submodule.coe_iInf]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun φ => (divPair a φ).isClosed_ker

/-- **`L²(TSD)` on the box** in the parity class `ParRow τ`: symmetric, trace-free and
divergence-free on `Q`. -/
def boxTSD (τ : ℂ) : Submodule ℝ L2M := ParRow τ ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr ⊓ boxDiv

theorem isClosed_boxTSD (τ : ℂ) : IsClosed (boxTSD τ : Set L2M) :=
  (((isClosed_ParRow τ).inter isClosed_boxSym).inter isClosed_boxTr).inter isClosed_boxDiv

instance (τ : ℂ) : (boxTSD τ).HasOrthogonalProjection := by
  have : CompleteSpace (boxTSD τ) := (isClosed_boxTSD τ).completeSpace_coe
  infer_instance

theorem boxTSD_le (τ : ℂ) : boxTSD τ ≤ ParRow τ ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr := fun _ h => h.1

/-- **Trigonometric polynomials in a row-wise parity class that are symmetric and trace-free on
the box vanish.** The extensions of `A_{ab}` and `A_{ba}` (`a ≠ b`) have opposite parities in
`x_a`, and the diagonal entries have pairwise different parities; once symmetry and trace hold
on all of `𝕋³` (analytic continuation, `eq_zero_of_zeroOnBox_of_finite`), the parities force
every entry to vanish. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_parRow_of_finite {τ : ℂ} (hτ : τ ≠ 0) {A : L2M} (hP : A ∈ ParRow τ)
    (hs : A ∈ boxSym) (ht : A ∈ boxTr) (S : Finset Z3) (hS : ∀ k ∉ S, A k = 0) : A = 0 := by
  have hsym : ∀ k a b, A k (a, b) = A k (b, a) := by
    intro k a b
    have h0 := eq_zero_of_zeroOnBox_of_finite S (fun j hj => by
      simp [entry_apply, hS j hj]) (mem_boxSym.1 hs a b)
    have := congrArg (fun f : L2 Z3 ℂ => f k) h0
    simpa [sub_eq_zero] using this
  have htr : ∀ k, ∑ a, A k (a, a) = 0 := by
    intro k
    have h0 := eq_zero_of_zeroOnBox_of_finite S (fun j hj => by
      rw [lp_sum_apply]; simp [entry_apply, hS j hj]) (mem_boxTr.1 ht)
    have := congrArg (fun f : L2 Z3 ℂ => f k) h0
    simp only [lp_sum_apply, entry_apply, lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply] at this
    exact this
  refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
  ext ⟨a, b⟩
  simp only [lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply, PiLp.zero_apply]
  by_cases hab : a = b
  · subst hab
    have h1 := htr (refl a k)
    simp only [hP a k] at h1
    have h2 : ∑ c, colSign a c * A k (c, c) = 0 := by
      have : τ * ∑ c, colSign a c * A k (c, c) = 0 := by
        rw [Finset.mul_sum]; rw [← h1]; refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun c _ => by ring
      exact (mul_eq_zero.1 this).resolve_left hτ
    have h3 := htr k
    fin_cases a <;> simp [colSign, Fin.sum_univ_three] at h2 h3 ⊢ <;>
      linear_combination (h2 + h3) / 2
  · have h1 := hsym (refl a k) a b
    rw [hP a k a b, hP a k b a, hsym k b a] at h1
    have hc1 : colSign a b = -1 := by simp [colSign, hab]
    have hc2 : colSign a a = 1 := by simp [colSign]
    rw [hc1, hc2] at h1
    have : (2 * τ) * A k (a, b) = 0 := by linear_combination -h1
    exact (mul_eq_zero.1 this).resolve_left (mul_ne_zero two_ne_zero hτ)

end Parity

/-! ## The spectral splitting of `K*` -/

section Dynamics

/-- The state space `W = L²(V) × L²(M) × L²(M)` (Fourier side). -/
abbrev X := Tot L2V L2M L2M

/-- The generator `-L` of the periodic (and box) Hodge wave group. -/
abbrev Lg : X →ₗ.[ℝ] X := -periodicComplex.waveOp

/-- The fibre `x̂(k) ∈ ℂ³ × ℂ³ˣ³ × ℂ³ˣ³` of a state at the mode `k`. -/
abbrev fib (y : X) (k : Z3) : Fib := fibIso.symm y k

theorem fib_add (y z : X) (k : Z3) : fib (y + z) k = fib y k + fib z k := by
  simp [fib]

theorem fib_smul (r : ℝ) (y : X) (k : Z3) : fib (r • y) k = r • fib y k := by
  simp [fib]

theorem fib_zero (k : Z3) : fib 0 k = 0 := by simp [fib]

theorem continuous_fib (k : Z3) : Continuous fun y : X => fib y k :=
  (lp.evalCLM ℝ (fun _ : Z3 => Fib) 2 k).continuous.comp fibIso.symm.continuous

/-- `-L` acts fibrewise by the symbols. -/
theorem fib_Lg (y : Lg.domain) (k : Z3) : fib (Lg y) k = waveSymK k (fib y k) := by
  rw [fib, neg_waveOp_eq, LinearIsometryEquiv.symm_apply_apply, mulOp_apply]

/-- The eigenspace `N_ω = ker(L² + ω²)`, fibrewise `W_k² x̂(k) = -ω² x̂(k)`. -/
def Nω (ω : ℝ) : Submodule ℝ X where
  carrier := {y | ∀ k, waveSymK k (waveSymK k (fib y k)) = -(ω ^ 2) • fib y k}
  zero_mem' := by intro k; simp [fib_zero]
  add_mem' := by
    intro y z hy hz k
    simp only [mem_ofPred_eq] at hy hz
    rw [fib_add, _root_.map_add, _root_.map_add, hy k, hz k, smul_add]
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r y hy k
    simp only [mem_ofPred_eq] at hy
    rw [fib_smul, _root_.map_smul, _root_.map_smul, hy k, smul_comm]

theorem mem_Nω {ω : ℝ} {y : X} :
    y ∈ Nω ω ↔ ∀ k, waveSymK k (waveSymK k (fib y k)) = -(ω ^ 2) • fib y k := Iff.rfl

theorem isClosed_Nω (ω : ℝ) : IsClosed (Nω ω : Set X) := by
  have e : (Nω ω : Set X) = ⋂ k, {y | waveSymK k (waveSymK k (fib y k)) = -(ω ^ 2) • fib y k} := by
    ext y; simp [mem_Nω]
  rw [e]
  exact isClosed_iInter fun k => isClosed_eq
    ((waveSymK k).continuous.comp ((waveSymK k).continuous.comp (continuous_fib k)))
    ((continuous_const_smul (-(ω ^ 2))).comp (continuous_fib k))

instance (ω : ℝ) : (Nω ω).HasOrthogonalProjection := by
  have : CompleteSpace (Nω ω) := (isClosed_Nω ω).completeSpace_coe
  infer_instance

/-- On `N_ω`, `‖W_k x̂(k)‖ = ω ‖x̂(k)‖`. -/
theorem norm_sq_waveSymK_of_mem {ω : ℝ} {y : X} (hy : y ∈ Nω ω) (k : Z3) :
    ‖waveSymK k (fib y k)‖ ^ 2 = ω ^ 2 * ‖fib y k‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [← real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, waveSymK, waveSym_skew, ← waveSymK, hy k, inner_smul_right,
    real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]
  ring

/-- `N_ω ⊆ D(L)`. -/
theorem mem_domain_of_mem_Nω {ω : ℝ} {y : X} (hy : y ∈ Nω ω) : y ∈ Lg.domain := by
  rw [mem_domain_neg_waveOp_iff]
  change fibIso.symm y ∈ mulDomain waveSymK
  rw [mem_mulDomain, memℓp_two_iff]
  have : (fun k => ‖waveSymK k (fibIso.symm y k)‖ ^ 2) = fun k => ω ^ 2 * ‖fibIso.symm y k‖ ^ 2 :=
    funext fun k => norm_sq_waveSymK_of_mem hy k
  rw [this]
  exact (summable_norm_sq_L2 (fibIso.symm y)).mul_left _

/-- `L N_ω ⊆ N_ω`. -/
theorem Lg_mem_Nω {ω : ℝ} (y : Lg.domain) (hy : (y : X) ∈ Nω ω) : Lg y ∈ Nω ω := by
  intro k
  rw [fib_Lg, hy k, _root_.map_smul]

/-- `L² = -ω²` on `N_ω`. -/
theorem Lg_Lg_of_mem_Nω {ω : ℝ} (y : Lg.domain) (hy : (y : X) ∈ Nω ω) :
    Lg ⟨Lg y, mem_domain_of_mem_Nω (Lg_mem_Nω y hy)⟩ = -(ω ^ 2) • (y : X) := by
  apply fibIso.symm.injective
  refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
  change fib _ k = fib _ k
  rw [fib_Lg, fib_smul]
  change waveSymK k (fib (Lg y) k) = _
  rw [fib_Lg, hy k]

/-- **The projection onto a reducing subspace preserves `N_ω`**: it commutes with `L`, hence
with `L²`. -/
theorem starProjection_mem_Nω (K' : Submodule ℝ X) [K'.HasOrthogonalProjection]
    (hK : ∀ t, ∀ x ∈ K', periodicGroup.S t x ∈ K') {ω : ℝ} {y : X} (hy : y ∈ Nω ω) :
    K'.starProjection y ∈ Nω ω := by
  set y' : Lg.domain := ⟨y, mem_domain_of_mem_Nω hy⟩
  obtain ⟨h1, e1⟩ := reducing_of_invariant periodicGroup K' hK y'
  set z : Lg.domain := ⟨Lg y', mem_domain_of_mem_Nω (Lg_mem_Nω y' hy)⟩
  obtain ⟨h2, e2⟩ := reducing_of_invariant periodicGroup K' hK z
  have e3 : Lg z = -(ω ^ 2) • y := Lg_Lg_of_mem_Nω y' hy
  intro k
  have a1 : waveSymK k (fib (K'.starProjection y) k) = fib (K'.starProjection (Lg y')) k := by
    rw [← fib_Lg ⟨_, h1⟩, e1]
  have a2 : waveSymK k (fib (K'.starProjection (Lg y')) k) =
      fib (K'.starProjection (Lg z)) k := by
    rw [← fib_Lg ⟨_, h2⟩, e2]
  rw [a1, a2, e3, _root_.map_smul, fib_smul]

/-- **The `N_ω`-component of a datum in a reducing subspace stays in it.** -/
theorem starProjection_Nω_mem (K' : Submodule ℝ X) [K'.HasOrthogonalProjection]
    (hK : ∀ t, ∀ x ∈ K', periodicGroup.S t x ∈ K') (ω : ℝ) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ K') :
    (Nω ω).starProjection x ∈ K' := by
  have hPy : K'.starProjection ((Nω ω).starProjection x) ∈ Nω ω :=
    starProjection_mem_Nω K' hK ((Nω ω).starProjection_apply_mem x)
  have hx' : K'.starProjection x = x := K'.starProjection_eq_self_iff.2 hx
  have key : (Nω ω).starProjection x = K'.starProjection ((Nω ω).starProjection x) := by
    refine Submodule.eq_starProjection_of_mem_of_inner_eq_zero hPy fun w hw => ?_
    have hw' : K'.starProjection w ∈ Nω ω := starProjection_mem_Nω K' hK hw
    calc ⟪x - K'.starProjection ((Nω ω).starProjection x), w⟫
        = ⟪K'.starProjection (x - (Nω ω).starProjection x), w⟫ := by
          rw [_root_.map_sub, hx']
      _ = ⟪x - (Nω ω).starProjection x, K'.starProjection w⟫ :=
          Submodule.inner_starProjection_left_eq_right _ _ _
      _ = 0 := (Nω ω).starProjection_inner_eq_zero x _ hw'
  rw [key]
  exact K'.starProjection_apply_mem _

/-- Only finitely many modes have a given frequency. -/
theorem finite_freq (ω : ℝ) : {k : Z3 | ‖freq k‖ = ω}.Finite := by
  set N : ℤ := ⌈ω⌉
  refine (Set.Finite.pi (t := fun _ : Fin 3 => Icc (-N) N) fun _ => finite_Icc _ _).subset ?_
  intro k hk j _
  have h1 : |freq k j| ≤ ‖freq k‖ := by
    have := PiLp.norm_apply_le (freq k) j
    rwa [Real.norm_eq_abs] at this
  have h2 : freq k j = 2 * Real.pi * k j := rfl
  have hpi : (1 : ℝ) ≤ 2 * Real.pi := by nlinarith [Real.two_le_pi]
  have h3 : |(k j : ℝ)| ≤ ω := by
    have : |(k j : ℝ)| ≤ 2 * Real.pi * |(k j : ℝ)| := le_mul_of_one_le_left (abs_nonneg _) hpi
    calc |(k j : ℝ)| ≤ 2 * Real.pi * |(k j : ℝ)| := this
      _ = |freq k j| := by
          rw [h2, abs_mul, abs_of_pos (show (0 : ℝ) < 2 * Real.pi by positivity)]
      _ ≤ ω := hk ▸ h1
  have h4 : |(k j : ℝ)| ≤ (N : ℝ) := h3.trans (Int.le_ceil ω)
  rw [← Int.cast_abs, Int.cast_le] at h4
  exact abs_le.1 h4

/-- **The non-stationary modes of `K` vanish**: an element of `K = {0} × S1 × S2` lying in the
eigenspace `N_ω`, `ω > 0`, is zero. It is a trigonometric polynomial (finitely many modes have
`|ξ_k| = ω`), so `eq_zero_of_parRow_of_finite` applies to `E` and to `B`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_mem_Kc_Nω {S1 S2 : Submodule ℝ L2M} (hS1 : S1 ≤ ParRow 1 ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr)
    (hS2 : S2 ≤ ParRow (-1) ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr) {ω : ℝ} (hω : 0 < ω) {y : X}
    (hy : y ∈ Kc L2V S1 S2) (hN : y ∈ Nω ω) : y = 0 := by
  set S := (finite_freq ω).toFinset
  have hfib : ∀ k ∉ S, fib y k = 0 := fun k hk =>
    eq_zero_of_waveSym_sq hω (fun h => hk ((finite_freq ω).mem_toFinset.2 h)) (hN k)
  rw [mem_Kc] at hy
  obtain ⟨h0, hE, hB⟩ := hy
  have hcoord : ∀ k ∉ S, (tot _ _ _ y).2.1 k = 0 ∧ (tot _ _ _ y).2.2 k = 0 := by
    intro k hk
    have := congrArg (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3) (hfib k hk)
    rw [tot_fibIso_symm_apply, _root_.map_zero] at this
    exact ⟨congrArg (fun p => p.2.1) this, congrArg (fun p => p.2.2) this⟩
  have hE0 := eq_zero_of_parRow_of_finite one_ne_zero (hS1 hE).1.1 (hS1 hE).1.2 (hS1 hE).2 S
    fun k hk => (hcoord k hk).1
  have hB0 := eq_zero_of_parRow_of_finite (neg_ne_zero.2 one_ne_zero) (hS2 hB).1.1 (hS2 hB).1.2
    (hS2 hB).2 S fun k hk => (hcoord k hk).2
  apply (tot L2V L2M L2M).injective
  rw [_root_.map_zero]
  exact Prod.ext h0 (Prod.ext hE0 hB0)

/-- **Every datum of `K*` is killed by every symbol**: `W_k x̂(k) = 0` for all `k`. For
`|ξ_k| = ω > 0`, the `N_ω`-component of `x` lies in `K*` (`starProjection_Nω_mem`) and in `K`,
hence vanishes; testing `x ⊥ N_ω` against the single mode `W_k² x̂(k) ∈ N_ω` gives
`‖W_k x̂(k)‖² = 0`. -/
theorem waveSym_eq_zero_of_mem_Kmax {S1 S2 : Submodule ℝ L2M} [S1.HasOrthogonalProjection]
    [S2.HasOrthogonalProjection] (hS1 : S1 ≤ ParRow 1 ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr)
    (hS2 : S2 ≤ ParRow (-1) ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ Kmax periodicGroup (Kc L2V S1 S2)) (k : Z3) : waveSymK k (fib x k) = 0 := by
  by_cases h0 : ‖freq k‖ = 0
  · rw [waveSymK, norm_eq_zero.1 h0, waveSym_zero]
  have hω : 0 < ‖freq k‖ := lt_of_le_of_ne (norm_nonneg _) (Ne.symm h0)
  set ω := ‖freq k‖
  have hK' : ∀ t, ∀ y ∈ Kmax periodicGroup (Kc L2V S1 S2),
      periodicGroup.S t y ∈ Kmax periodicGroup (Kc L2V S1 S2) := fun t y h => S_mem_Kmax h t
  have hy := starProjection_Nω_mem _ hK' ω hx
  have hy0 := eq_zero_of_mem_Kc_Nω hS1 hS2 hω (Kmax_le hy) ((Nω ω).starProjection_apply_mem x)
  have hxo : x ∈ (Nω ω)ᗮ := (Submodule.starProjection_apply_eq_zero_iff (Nω ω)).1 hy0
  set u := fib x k
  set v := waveSymK k (waveSymK k u)
  have hz : fibIso (lp.single 2 k v) ∈ Nω ω := by
    intro j
    rw [fib, LinearIsometryEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
    by_cases hj : j = k
    · subst hj
      simp only [lp.single_apply_self]
      exact waveSym_four _ _
    · simp [lp.single_apply, hj]
  have hi := Submodule.inner_right_of_mem_orthogonal hz hxo
  rw [← LinearIsometryEquiv.apply_symm_apply fibIso x, LinearIsometryEquiv.inner_map_map,
    lp.inner_single_left] at hi
  change ⟪v, u⟫ = 0 at hi
  have e : ⟪v, u⟫ = -⟪waveSymK k u, waveSymK k u⟫ := waveSym_skew (freq k) (waveSymK k u) u
  have h2 : ⟪waveSymK k u, waveSymK k u⟫ = 0 := by linarith
  rwa [real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, sq_eq_zero_iff, norm_eq_zero] at h2

/-- `exp(tA) v = v` if `A v = 0`. -/
theorem exp_smul_apply_of_eq_zero {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [CompleteSpace E] (A : E →L[ℝ] E) {v : E} (hv : A v = 0) (t : ℝ) : exp (t • A) v = v := by
  have hd : ∀ s : ℝ, HasDerivAt (fun s : ℝ => exp (s • A) v) 0 s := by
    intro s
    have h := hasDerivAt_exp_smul_apply A v s
    have hc : Commute A (exp (s • A)) := ((Commute.refl A).smul_right s).exp_right
    have : A (exp (s • A) v) = 0 := by
      change (A * exp (s • A)) v = 0
      rw [hc.eq]
      change exp (s • A) (A v) = 0
      rw [hv, _root_.map_zero]
    rwa [this] at h
  have := is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero (fun s => (hd s).differentiableAt) (fun s => (hd s).deriv) t 0
  rw [this, zero_smul, exp_zero]
  rfl

/-- A state killed by every symbol is stationary. -/
theorem stationary_of_waveSym_eq_zero {x : X} (h : ∀ k, waveSymK k (fib x k) = 0) (t : ℝ) :
    periodicGroup.S t x = x := by
  apply fibIso.symm.injective
  refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
  rw [periodicGroup_apply]
  exact exp_smul_apply_of_eq_zero _ (h k) t

/-- **Prop 4.17 on the box with the thesis' boundary conditions: only static data propagate.**
For any closed `S1 ≤ ParRow 1 ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr` and `S2 ≤ ParRow (-1) ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr` (in
particular for `L²(TSD)` on the box, `mem_Kmax_boxTSD_iff`), a datum lies in the largest
invariant subspace `K*` of `K = {0} × S1 × S2` iff it lies in `K` and is stationary.

Correction: this answers the question left open in `Feec.Ch4.BoundedSalvageMax` for the box:
`K*` contains no non-stationary datum, so on `Q` the corrected Prop 4.17
(`Feec.Constraints.prop_4_17_max`) has only trivial content. -/
theorem mem_Kmax_iff {S1 S2 : Submodule ℝ L2M} [S1.HasOrthogonalProjection]
    [S2.HasOrthogonalProjection] (hS1 : S1 ≤ ParRow 1 ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr)
    (hS2 : S2 ≤ ParRow (-1) ⊓ boxSym ⊓ boxTr) (x : X) :
    x ∈ Kmax periodicGroup (Kc L2V S1 S2) ↔
      x ∈ Kc L2V S1 S2 ∧ ∀ t, periodicGroup.S t x = x := by
  refine ⟨fun hx => ⟨Kmax_le hx, stationary_of_waveSym_eq_zero
    (waveSym_eq_zero_of_mem_Kmax hS1 hS2 hx)⟩, fun ⟨hK, hs⟩ t => ?_⟩
  rw [hs t]; exact hK

/-- `freq k = 0` only at `k = 0`. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_freq_eq_zero {k : Z3} (h : freq k = 0) : k = 0 := by
  ext j
  have := congrArg (fun ξ : Freq => ξ j) h
  simp only [freq, PiLp.zero_apply] at this
  have hpi : (2 * Real.pi) ≠ 0 := by positivity
  have : (k j : ℝ) = 0 := (mul_eq_zero.1 this).resolve_left hpi
  exact_mod_cast this

/-- In `ParRow 1` the mean (`k = 0` mode) vanishes: every `E_{ab}` is odd in some variable. -/
theorem parRow_one_zero_mode {A : L2M} (hA : A ∈ ParRow 1) : A 0 = 0 := by
  ext ⟨a, b⟩
  have h := hA (b + 1) 0 a b
  rw [refl_zero] at h
  have hc : colSign (b + 1) b = -1 := by
    fin_cases b <;> simp [colSign]
  rw [hc] at h
  simp only [PiLp.zero_apply]
  linear_combination h / 2

/-- **The thesis' `K` on the box**: `K* = {(0, 0, B₀) : B₀ ∈ L²(TSD), curl B₀ = 0}` for
`K = {0} × L²(TSD) × L²(TSD)` with the boundary conditions of the complex
`H̊¹(V) → H̊(curl; M) → L²(M)` (encoded by `ParV`, `ParRow 1`, `ParRow (-1)`). In particular
`S1* = 0`: no nonzero electric datum propagates.

See [QuennevilleBelair2015, §4.10, Prop 4.17]. -/
theorem mem_Kmax_boxTSD_iff (x : X) :
    x ∈ Kmax periodicGroup (Kc L2V (boxTSD 1) (boxTSD (-1))) ↔
      ∃ B ∈ boxTSD (-1), (∀ k, curlSym (freq k) (B k) = 0) ∧ x = ini L2V 0 B := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    have hW := waveSym_eq_zero_of_mem_Kmax (boxTSD_le 1) (boxTSD_le (-1)) hx
    have hK := Kmax_le hx
    rw [mem_Kc] at hK
    obtain ⟨h0, hE, hB⟩ := hK
    have hcomp : ∀ k, divSym (freq k) ((tot _ _ _ x).2.1 k) = 0 ∧
        curlSym (freq k) ((tot _ _ _ x).2.2 k) = 0 ∧
        curlSym (freq k) ((tot _ _ _ x).2.1 k) = 0 := by
      intro k
      have := congrArg (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3) (hW k)
      rw [waveSymK, tot_waveSym, tot_fibIso_symm_apply, _root_.map_zero, h0] at this
      simp only [lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply, _root_.map_zero, neg_zero, zero_sub,
        Prod.mk_eq_zero, neg_eq_zero] at this
      exact ⟨this.1, this.2.1, this.2.2⟩
    have hE0 : (tot _ _ _ x).2.1 = 0 := by
      refine lp.ext (funext fun k => ?_)
      by_cases hk : freq k = 0
      · rw [eq_zero_of_freq_eq_zero hk, lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
        exact parRow_one_zero_mode hE.1.1.1
      · have hl := lagrange (freq k) ((tot _ _ _ x).2.1 k)
        rw [← norm_curlSym, ← norm_divSym, (hcomp k).1, (hcomp k).2.2, norm_zero] at hl
        have : ‖freq k‖ ^ 2 * ‖(tot _ _ _ x).2.1 k‖ ^ 2 = 0 := by rw [← hl]; simp
        rcases mul_eq_zero.1 this with h | h
        · exact absurd (norm_eq_zero.1 (pow_eq_zero_iff two_ne_zero |>.1 h)) hk
        · rw [lp.coeFn_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
          exact norm_eq_zero.1 (pow_eq_zero_iff two_ne_zero |>.1 h)
    refine ⟨(tot _ _ _ x).2.2, hB, fun k => (hcomp k).2.1, ?_⟩
    apply (tot L2V L2M L2M).injective
    rw [tot_ini]
    exact Prod.ext h0 (Prod.ext hE0 rfl)
  · rintro ⟨B, hB, hc, rfl⟩
    rw [mem_Kmax_iff (boxTSD_le 1) (boxTSD_le (-1))]
    refine ⟨by rw [mem_Kc, tot_ini]; exact ⟨rfl, (boxTSD 1).zero_mem, hB⟩,
      stationary_of_waveSym_eq_zero fun k => ?_⟩
    apply (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective
    rw [waveSymK, tot_waveSym, tot_fibIso_symm_apply, tot_ini, _root_.map_zero]
    simp [hc k]

end Dynamics

/-! ## The box dynamics: the periodic group preserves the parity space -/

section BoxDynamics

/-- `ξ_{R_i k}`: reflection of the `i`-th frequency. -/
theorem freq_refl_apply (i : Fin 3) (k : Z3) (j : Fin 3) :
    freq (refl i k) j = if j = i then -freq k j else freq k j := by
  by_cases h : j = i
  · subst h; simp [freq, refl]
  · simp [freq, refl, h]

/-- The row-wise sign action `A_{ab} ↦ τ colSign i b A_{ab}` on a fibre. -/
def rowSgn (τ : ℂ) (i : Fin 3) : Mat3 →L[ℝ] Mat3 :=
  LinearMap.toContinuousLinearMap
    { toFun := fun M => mat fun a b => τ * colSign i b * M (a, b)
      map_add' := fun M N => by ext ⟨a, b⟩; simp [mul_add]
      map_smul' := fun r M => by ext ⟨a, b⟩; simp [Complex.real_smul]; ring }

@[simp] theorem rowSgn_apply (τ : ℂ) (i : Fin 3) (M : Mat3) (a b : Fin 3) :
    rowSgn τ i M (a, b) = τ * colSign i b * M (a, b) := rfl

/-- The reflection `x_i ↦ -x_i` on a fibre of the state `(σ, E, B)`, with the parities of the
thesis' complex: `σ` odd, `E ∈ ParRow 1`, `B ∈ ParRow (-1)`. -/
def reflFib (i : Fin 3) : Fib →L[ℝ] Fib :=
  (Constraints.totL (W0 := Vec3) (W1 := Mat3) (W2 := Mat3)).symm.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L
    ((-ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ Vec3).prodMap ((rowSgn 1 i).prodMap (rowSgn (-1) i))) ∘L
    (Constraints.totL (W0 := Vec3) (W1 := Mat3) (W2 := Mat3)).toContinuousLinearMap

theorem tot_reflFib (i : Fin 3) (x : Fib) :
    tot _ _ _ (reflFib i x) =
      (-(tot _ _ _ x).1, rowSgn 1 i (tot _ _ _ x).2.1, rowSgn (-1) i (tot _ _ _ x).2.2) := by
  simp [reflFib]; rfl

/-- **The wave symbol intertwines the reflections**: `W_{R_i k} ρ_i = ρ_i W_k`. -/
theorem waveSym_refl (i : Fin 3) (k : Z3) (x : Fib) :
    waveSym (freq (refl i k)) (reflFib i x) = reflFib i (waveSym (freq k) x) := by
  apply (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective
  rw [tot_waveSym, tot_reflFib, tot_reflFib, tot_waveSym]
  obtain ⟨σ, u, ρ⟩ := tot _ _ _ x
  simp only
  refine Prod.ext ?_ (Prod.ext ?_ ?_)
  · ext a
    simp only [PiLp.neg_apply, divSym_apply, rowSgn_apply, freq_refl_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
    fin_cases i <;> simp [colSign] <;> ring
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩
    simp only [PiLp.neg_apply, PiLp.sub_apply, gradSym_apply, curlSym_apply, jM_apply,
      curlR_apply, cross, rowSgn_apply, freq_refl_apply]
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases b <;> simp [colSign] <;> ring
  · ext ⟨a, b⟩
    simp only [curlSym_apply, jM_apply, curlR_apply, cross, rowSgn_apply, freq_refl_apply]
    fin_cases i <;> fin_cases b <;> simp [colSign] <;> ring

/-- The parity space of the box model: `x̂(R_i k) = ρ_i x̂(k)`. -/
def Par : Submodule ℝ X where
  carrier := {x | ∀ i k, fib x (refl i k) = reflFib i (fib x k)}
  zero_mem' := by intro i k; simp [fib_zero]
  add_mem' := by
    intro x y hx hy i k
    simp only [mem_ofPred_eq] at hx hy
    rw [fib_add, fib_add, hx, hy, _root_.map_add]
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r x hx i k
    simp only [mem_ofPred_eq] at hx
    rw [fib_smul, fib_smul, hx, _root_.map_smul]

/-- `Par = ParV × ParRow 1 × ParRow (-1)`. -/
theorem mem_Par_iff (x : X) :
    x ∈ Par ↔ (tot _ _ _ x).1 ∈ ParV ∧ (tot _ _ _ x).2.1 ∈ ParRow 1 ∧
      (tot _ _ _ x).2.2 ∈ ParRow (-1) := by
  have e : ∀ i k, (fib x (refl i k) = reflFib i (fib x k)) ↔
      ((tot _ _ _ x).1 (refl i k) = -(tot _ _ _ x).1 k ∧
        (tot _ _ _ x).2.1 (refl i k) = rowSgn 1 i ((tot _ _ _ x).2.1 k) ∧
        (tot _ _ _ x).2.2 (refl i k) = rowSgn (-1) i ((tot _ _ _ x).2.2 k)) := by
    intro i k
    rw [← (tot Vec3 Mat3 Mat3).injective.eq_iff, tot_reflFib, fib, fib,
      tot_fibIso_symm_apply, tot_fibIso_symm_apply]
    simp only [Prod.mk.injEq]
  change (∀ i k, fib x (refl i k) = reflFib i (fib x k)) ↔ _
  simp only [e]
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine ⟨fun i k a => ?_, fun i k a b => ?_, fun i k a b => ?_⟩
    · rw [(h i k).1]; rfl
    · rw [(h i k).2.1]; rfl
    · rw [(h i k).2.2]; rfl
  · rintro ⟨h0, h1, h2⟩ i k
    refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
    · ext a; exact h0 i k a
    · ext ⟨a, b⟩; exact h1 i k a b
    · ext ⟨a, b⟩; exact h2 i k a b

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- **The box evolution is well defined**: the periodic Hodge wave group preserves the parity
space `Par` of the box model, so its restriction is a group on the box state space. -/
theorem periodicGroup_mem_Par {x : X} (hx : x ∈ Par) (t : ℝ) : periodicGroup.S t x ∈ Par := by
  intro i k
  have hsc : SemiconjBy (reflFib i) (t • waveSymK k) (t • waveSymK (refl i k)) := by
    ext1 y
    change reflFib i ((t • waveSymK k) y) = (t • waveSymK (refl i k)) (reflFib i y)
    simp only [_root_.smul_apply, _root_.map_smul, waveSymK]
    rw [waveSym_refl]
  let _ : NormedAlgebra ℚ (Fib →L[ℝ] Fib) := NormedAlgebra.restrictScalars ℚ ℝ (Fib →L[ℝ] Fib)
  have hexp : reflFib i * exp (t • waveSymK k) = exp (t • waveSymK (refl i k)) * reflFib i :=
    SemiconjBy.exp_right hsc
  change fibIso.symm (periodicGroup.S t x) (refl i k) =
    reflFib i (fibIso.symm (periodicGroup.S t x) k)
  rw [periodicGroup_apply, periodicGroup_apply]
  have hxk : fibIso.symm x (refl i k) = reflFib i (fibIso.symm x k) := hx i k
  rw [hxk]
  exact (congrArg (fun A : Fib →L[ℝ] Fib => A (fibIso.symm x k)) hexp).symm

end BoxDynamics

end Feec.Box
